{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"outage","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Concurrent recovery can invalidate the live cleanup's frozen-process assumption, allowing a stale signal to kill an unrelated process if PID reuse and inspection failures also occur."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"test","trigger":"normal","reason":"The default test preload replaces the real boot-identity reader, leaving its production paths untested without establishing a current runtime defect."}]}